## Run everything

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Each service is built from its own folder under `services/` and published on the port listed above.
[[- if or .Postgres .MySQL .Mongo .Kafka .RabbitMQ ]]

Shared infrastructure started by `compose.yaml`:
[[ if .Postgres ]]
- PostgreSQL with one database per service ([[ range $i, $db := .Postgres ]][[ if $i ]], [[ end ]]`[[ $db ]]`[[ end ]]), user `app` / `app`
[[- end ]]
[[- if .MySQL ]]
- MySQL with one database per service ([[ range $i, $db := .MySQL ]][[ if $i ]], [[ end ]]`[[ $db ]]`[[ end ]]), user `app` / `app`
[[- end ]]
[[- if .Mongo ]]
- MongoDB with one database per service
[[- end ]]
[[- if .Kafka ]]
- Kafka at `kafka:9092`
[[- end ]]
[[- if .RabbitMQ ]]
- RabbitMQ at `rabbitmq:5672` (management UI on http://localhost:15672)
[[- end ]]
[[- end ]]

## Working on one service

Every service keeps its own README, build files and tests in `services/<name>`, and can be
built and run on its own from that folder.

CI builds only the services whose folder changed.
